IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`

-- coa25-communications.l4: Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 37, "Sending or supplying documents or
-- information": ss 1143 to 1148 (lines 16293-16340 of ukpga-2006-46.txt). Layer 1: the law, objectively.
--
-- SOURCE. A plain-text rendering of the Act from legislation.gov.uk made by a converter script; it is not the
-- official text and nothing here is "verified against the official text". Quote lines are checked by srcrefs.py.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER (the rule of 2026-10-29, assumed, not ruled by a lawyer; NOTES.md, "Reading a result").
--   JUST TRUE   the text says yes.
--   JUST FALSE  the text says no in its own words: -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "<quoted words>"
--   NOTHING     the text does not decide: -- NOTHING-kind (<why>), <why> being one of: silent, list not closed,
--               includes, undefined term, points outside the text, limited by its own wording.
--   A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Answers that Schedules 4 and 5 (coa29), the keel (working day, body corporate) and other parts (Part 35, s 1121)
-- give are INPUTS under the names PLAN.md section 4 gives them. Every name below begins with its section label.

§ `Part 37: companies, supplementary provisions`

§§ `Sending or supplying documents or information`

-- ---- s 1143: The company communications provisions ------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `s 1143 provision` IS ONE OF
    `s 1143 a section of the Companies Act 2006` HAS `s 1143 section number` IS A NUMBER
    `s 1143 a Schedule to the Companies Act 2006` HAS `s 1143 Schedule number` IS A NUMBER

-- src:16294 | 1143 The company communications provisions
-- src:16295 | (1) The provisions of sections 1144 to 1148 and Schedules 4 and 5 (“the company communications provisions”) have effect for the purposes of any provision of the Companies Acts that authorises or requires documents or information to be sent or supplied by or to a company.
@ref s 1143(1) The company communications provisions (src:16294-16295)
GIVEN provision IS A `s 1143 provision`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1143(1) the provision is one of the company communications provisions` MEANS
    CONSIDER provision
    WHEN `s 1143 a section of the Companies Act 2006` n THEN
        IF n AT LEAST 1144 AND n AT MOST 1148
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The provisions of sections 1144 to 1148 and Schedules 4 and 5 (“the company communications provisions”)" (a defined term)
    WHEN `s 1143 a Schedule to the Companies Act 2006` n THEN
        IF n EQUALS 4 OR n EQUALS 5
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The provisions of sections 1144 to 1148 and Schedules 4 and 5 (“the company communications provisions”)" (a defined term)

-- src:16294 | 1143 The company communications provisions
-- src:16295 | (1) The provisions of sections 1144 to 1148 and Schedules 4 and 5 (“the company communications provisions”) have effect for the purposes of any provision of the Companies Acts that authorises or requires documents or information to be sent or supplied by or to a company.
@ref s 1143(1) The company communications provisions (src:16294-16295)
GIVEN `a provision of the Companies Acts authorises or requires documents or information to be sent or supplied by or to a company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1143(1) the company communications provisions have effect for the purposes of the provision` MEANS
    IF `a provision of the Companies Acts authorises or requires documents or information to be sent or supplied by or to a company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "have effect for the purposes of any provision of the Companies Acts that authorises or requires documents or information to be sent or supplied by or to a company"

-- src:16296 | (2) The company communications provisions have effect subject to any requirements imposed, or contrary provision made, by or under any enactment.
@ref s 1143(2) The company communications provisions have effect subject to contrary provision (src:16296)
GIVEN `a requirement is imposed, or contrary provision is made, by or under an enactment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1143(2) the company communications provisions yield to the other provision` MEANS
    IF `a requirement is imposed, or contrary provision is made, by or under an enactment`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "subject to any requirements imposed, or contrary provision made, by or under any enactment"

-- src:16297 | (3) In particular, in their application in relation to documents or information to be sent or supplied to the registrar, they have effect subject to the provisions of Part 35.
@ref s 1143(3) In their application to documents sent to the registrar, subject to Part 35 (src:16297)
GIVEN `the document or information is to be sent or supplied to the registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1143(3) the company communications provisions yield to Part 35` MEANS
    IF `the document or information is to be sent or supplied to the registrar`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in their application in relation to documents or information to be sent or supplied to the registrar"

-- src:16298 | (4) For the purposes of subsection (2), provision is not to be regarded as contrary to the company communications provisions by reason only of the fact that it expressly authorises a document or information to be sent or supplied in hard copy form, in electronic form or by means of a website.
@ref s 1143(4) Express authority to use hard copy, electronic form or a website is not contrary provision (src:16298)
GIVEN `the provision expressly authorises a document or information to be sent or supplied in hard copy form, in electronic form or by means of a website` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is some other reason why the provision is contrary to the company communications provisions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1143(4) the provision is regarded as contrary to the company communications provisions` MEANS
    IF `the provision expressly authorises a document or information to be sent or supplied in hard copy form, in electronic form or by means of a website`
       AND NOT `there is some other reason why the provision is contrary to the company communications provisions`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "provision is not to be regarded as contrary to the company communications provisions by reason only of the fact that it expressly authorises a document or information to be sent or supplied in hard copy form, in electronic form or by means of a website"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by reason only of the fact that it expressly authorises"

-- ---- s 1144: Sending or supplying documents or information ----------------------------------------------

DECLARE `s 1144 direction of the communication` IS ONE OF
    `s 1144 to a company by a person who is not a company`
    `s 1144 by a company to a person who is not a company`
    `s 1144 by one company to another company`

DECLARE `s 1144 schedule` IS ONE OF
    `s 1144 Schedule 4`
    `s 1144 Schedule 5`

-- src:16299 | 1144 Sending or supplying documents or information
-- src:16300 | (1) Documents or information to be sent or supplied to a company must be sent or supplied in accordance with the provisions of Schedule 4.
-- src:16301 | (2) Documents or information to be sent or supplied by a company must be sent or supplied in accordance with the provisions of Schedule 5.
-- src:16302 | (3) The provisions referred to in subsection (2) apply (and those referred to in subsection (1) do not apply) in relation to documents or information that are to be sent or supplied by one company to another.
@ref s 1144 Sending or supplying documents or information (src:16299-16302)
GIVEN direction IS A `s 1144 direction of the communication`
GIVETH A `s 1144 schedule`
`s 1144 the Schedule that governs the communication` MEANS
    CONSIDER direction
    WHEN `s 1144 to a company by a person who is not a company` THEN `s 1144 Schedule 4` -- (1)
    WHEN `s 1144 by a company to a person who is not a company` THEN `s 1144 Schedule 5` -- (2)
    WHEN `s 1144 by one company to another company` THEN `s 1144 Schedule 5` -- (3): Schedule 5 applies and Schedule 4 does not

-- src:16299 | 1144 Sending or supplying documents or information
-- src:16300 | (1) Documents or information to be sent or supplied to a company must be sent or supplied in accordance with the provisions of Schedule 4.
-- src:16301 | (2) Documents or information to be sent or supplied by a company must be sent or supplied in accordance with the provisions of Schedule 5.
-- src:16302 | (3) The provisions referred to in subsection (2) apply (and those referred to in subsection (1) do not apply) in relation to documents or information that are to be sent or supplied by one company to another.
@ref s 1144 Sending or supplying documents or information (src:16299-16302)
GIVEN direction IS A `s 1144 direction of the communication`
      `sch 4 the document or information has been sent or supplied to the company in accordance with Schedule 4` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `sch 5 the document or information has been sent or supplied by the company in accordance with Schedule 5` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1144 the document or information has been sent or supplied` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 1144 the Schedule that governs the communication` direction
    WHEN `s 1144 Schedule 4` THEN
        CONSIDER `sch 4 the document or information has been sent or supplied to the company in accordance with Schedule 4`
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Documents or information to be sent or supplied to a company must be sent or supplied in accordance with the provisions of Schedule 4" (a bare "must" not done: decided at this site, fork F5)
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): Schedule 4 (coa29) is not known
    WHEN `s 1144 Schedule 5` THEN
        CONSIDER `sch 5 the document or information has been sent or supplied by the company in accordance with Schedule 5`
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Documents or information to be sent or supplied by a company must be sent or supplied in accordance with the provisions of Schedule 5" (a bare "must" not done: decided at this site, fork F5)
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): Schedule 5 (coa29) is not known

-- ---- s 1145: Right to hard copy version ----------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `s 1145 holder` IS ONE OF
    `s 1145 a member of the company`
    `s 1145 a holder of the company's debentures`
    `s 1145 another person`

-- src:16303 | 1145 Right to hard copy version
-- src:16304 | (1) Where a member of a company or a holder of a company's debentures has received a document or information from the company otherwise than in hard copy form, he is entitled to require the company to send him a version of the document or information in hard copy form.
@ref s 1145(1) Right to hard copy version (src:16303-16304)
GIVEN holder IS A `s 1145 holder`
      `the document or information was received from the company otherwise than in hard copy form` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1145(1) the person is entitled to require the company to send a hard copy version` MEANS
    CONSIDER holder
    WHEN `s 1145 another person` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a member of a company or a holder of a company's debentures"
    OTHERWISE
        IF `the document or information was received from the company otherwise than in hard copy form`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a member of a company or a holder of a company's debentures has received a document or information from the company otherwise than in hard copy form" (a "where" that fails: the 2026-11-05 ruling)

-- "within 21 days of receipt of the request": the last day is the day of receipt plus 21 days (fork F4: the day of
-- receipt is day 0 and the 21st day after it is the last).
-- src:16305 | (2) The company must send the document or information in hard copy form within 21 days of receipt of the request from the member or debenture holder.
@ref s 1145(2) The company must send the hard copy within 21 days of receipt of the request (src:16305)
GIVEN `the date the company received the request` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 1145(2) the last day for sending the hard copy version` MEANS
    `the date the company received the request` PLUS 21

-- src:16305 | (2) The company must send the document or information in hard copy form within 21 days of receipt of the request from the member or debenture holder.
@ref s 1145(2) The company must send the hard copy within 21 days of receipt of the request (src:16305)
GIVEN `the date the company received the request` IS A DATE
      `the date the company sent the hard copy version` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1145(2) the company sent the hard copy version in time` MEANS
    IF `the date the company sent the hard copy version` LESS THAN `the date the company received the request`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text speaks of sending after receipt of the request
    ELSE IF `the date the company sent the hard copy version` AT MOST `s 1145(2) the last day for sending the hard copy version` `the date the company received the request`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The company must send the document or information in hard copy form within 21 days of receipt of the request" (a period the text fixes in its own words: the 2026-11-05 ruling)

-- src:16306 | (3) The company may not make a charge for providing the document or information in that form.
@ref s 1145(3) The company may not make a charge (src:16306)
GIVEN `the version is one that the person is entitled to require under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1145(3) the company may make a charge for providing the hard copy version` MEANS
    IF `the version is one that the person is entitled to require under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The company may not make a charge for providing the document or information in that form"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in that form": the version a member or debenture holder is entitled to require under subsection (1)

-- src:16303 | 1145 Right to hard copy version
-- src:16304 | (1) Where a member of a company or a holder of a company's debentures has received a document or information from the company otherwise than in hard copy form, he is entitled to require the company to send him a version of the document or information in hard copy form.
-- src:16305 | (2) The company must send the document or information in hard copy form within 21 days of receipt of the request from the member or debenture holder.
-- src:16306 | (3) The company may not make a charge for providing the document or information in that form.
@ref s 1145 Right to hard copy version (the whole section, for the offence in subsection (4)) (src:16303-16306)
GIVEN `s 1145(1) the person is entitled to require the company to send a hard copy version` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1145(2) the company sent the hard copy version in time` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the company made a charge for providing the version` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1145 the company has complied with this section` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 1145(1) the person is entitled to require the company to send a hard copy version`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE -- the duty does not engage, so nothing is left to fail (fork F5)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the person is not within subsection (1)
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the company made a charge for providing the version`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The company may not make a charge for providing the document or information in that form"
        ELSE `s 1145(2) the company sent the hard copy version in time`

-- src:16307 | (4) If a company fails to comply with this section, an offence is committed by the company and every officer of it who is in default.
@ref s 1145(4) Offence: the company (src:16307)
GIVEN `s 1145 the company has complied with this section` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1145(4) the company commits an offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 1145 the company has complied with this section`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company fails to comply with this section, an offence is committed by the company" (an "if" that is not met)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the company complied is not known

-- src:16307 | (4) If a company fails to comply with this section, an offence is committed by the company and every officer of it who is in default.
@ref s 1145(4) Offence: every officer of the company who is in default (src:16307)
GIVEN `s 1145 the company has complied with this section` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1145(4) an officer of the company commits an offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 1145 the company has complied with this section`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company fails to comply with this section, an offence is committed by ... every officer of it who is in default" (an "if" that is not met)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the company complied is not known
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN
        CONSIDER `s 1121 the officer is in default`
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every officer of it who is in default"
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the officer is in default is the answer of s 1121

-- src:16308 | (5) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 1145(5) Penalty for an offence under s 1145 (src:16308)
GIVEN guilty IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 1145(5) the penalty for an offence under s 1145` MEANS
    CONSIDER guilty
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        JUST (Penalty WITH `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction`
                           `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
                           `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1)
                           `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1)
                           `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE)
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is guilty is not known

-- The duty of subsection (2) as a regulative rule: the company must send the version within 21 days of receiving the
-- request. The member or debenture holder is the recipient: the rule is for one holder, given as a GIVEN party and
-- compared in a PROVIDED guard (a GIVEN named in an action matches any payload on main: dialects.md).
-- src:16305 | (2) The company must send the document or information in hard copy form within 21 days of receipt of the request from the member or debenture holder.
@ref s 1145(2) The company must send the hard copy within 21 days of receipt of the request (src:16305)
GIVEN holder IS A Party
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Action of a party`
`s 1145(2) the company must send the hard copy version within 21 days` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `Action of a party` OF Company, recipient, "send the document or information in hard copy form"
         PROVIDED recipient EQUALS holder
    WITHIN 21
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "s 1145(2): the hard copy version was not sent within 21 days of receipt of the request"

-- ---- s 1146: Requirement of authentication --------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:16309 | 1146 Requirement of authentication
-- src:16310 | (1) This section applies in relation to the authentication of a document or information sent or supplied by a person to a company.
@ref s 1146(1) Authentication of a document or information sent or supplied by a person to a company (src:16309-16310)
GIVEN `the document or information is sent or supplied by a person to a company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1146(1) the section applies to the authentication of the document or information` MEANS
    IF `the document or information is sent or supplied by a person to a company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the authentication of a document or information sent or supplied by a person to a company" (a scope limit with no "only": the 2026-11-05 ruling)

-- src:16311 | (2) A document or information sent or supplied in hard copy form is sufficiently authenticated if it is signed by the person sending or supplying it.
@ref s 1146(2) A hard copy document is sufficiently authenticated if signed (src:16311)
GIVEN `the document or information is signed by the person sending or supplying it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1146(2) the hard copy document or information is sufficiently authenticated` MEANS
    IF `the document or information is signed by the person sending or supplying it`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is sufficiently authenticated if it is signed by the person sending or supplying it" (an "if" that is not met: marginal reading (a))

-- src:16312 | (3) A document or information sent or supplied in electronic form is sufficiently authenticated—
-- src:16313 | (a) if the identity of the sender is confirmed in a manner specified by the company, or
-- src:16314 | (b) where no such manner has been specified by the company, if the communication contains or is accompanied by a statement of the identity of the sender and the company has no reason to doubt the truth of that statement.
@ref s 1146(3) An electronic document is sufficiently authenticated (src:16312-16314)
GIVEN `the company has specified a manner of confirming the identity of the sender` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the identity of the sender is confirmed in the manner the company specified` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the communication contains or is accompanied by a statement of the identity of the sender` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has no reason to doubt the truth of that statement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1146(3) the electronic document or information is sufficiently authenticated` MEANS
    IF `the company has specified a manner of confirming the identity of the sender`
    THEN IF `the identity of the sender is confirmed in the manner the company specified`
         THEN JUST TRUE -- (a)
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) if the identity of the sender is confirmed in a manner specified by the company" (an "if" that is not met; limb (b) is for "where no such manner has been specified")
    ELSE IF `the communication contains or is accompanied by a statement of the identity of the sender`
            AND `the company has no reason to doubt the truth of that statement`
         THEN JUST TRUE -- (b)
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) where no such manner has been specified by the company, if the communication contains or is accompanied by a statement of the identity of the sender and the company has no reason to doubt the truth of that statement" (an "if" that is not met)

-- src:16315 | (4) Where a document or information is sent or supplied by one person on behalf of another, nothing in this section affects any provision of the company's articles under which the company may require reasonable evidence of the authority of the former to act on behalf of the latter.
@ref s 1146(4) A document sent on behalf of another: the articles may require evidence of authority (src:16315)
GIVEN `the document or information is sent or supplied by one person on behalf of another` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the articles provide that the company may require reasonable evidence of the authority of the former to act on behalf of the latter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1146(4) the section affects the provision of the articles requiring evidence of authority` MEANS
    IF `the document or information is sent or supplied by one person on behalf of another`
       AND `the articles provide that the company may require reasonable evidence of the authority of the former to act on behalf of the latter`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "nothing in this section affects any provision of the company's articles under which the company may require reasonable evidence of the authority of the former to act on behalf of the latter"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a document or information is sent or supplied by one person on behalf of another"

-- ---- s 1147: Deemed delivery of documents and information -----------------------------------------------
-- REPRESENTATION (fork F7). The text counts HOURS ("48 hours after it was posted") and ignores "any part of a day
-- that is not a working day", so a point in time is a day and an hour of that day (0 to 24). Whether a day is a
-- working day is the keel's answer (s 1173(1), PLAN.md section 4.1), taken here as an input: a function from a date
-- to BOOLEAN. PLAN.md section 4.2 types the answer other parts want, `s 1147 the day the document is treated as
-- delivered`, as a DATE: the day of the instant is that answer (the text itself gives an instant).

DECLARE `s 1147 instant` HAS
    `s 1147 day of the instant` IS A DATE
    `s 1147 hour of the day` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `s 1147 how the document or information was sent` IS ONE OF
    `s 1147 by post to an address in the United Kingdom`
    `s 1147 by electronic means`
    `s 1147 by means of a website`
    `s 1147 in another way`

-- src:16329 | (5) In calculating a period of hours for the purposes of this section, no account shall be taken of any part of a day that is not a working day.
@ref s 1147(5) In calculating a period of hours, no account is taken of any part of a day that is not a working day (src:16329)
GIVEN start IS A `s 1147 instant`
      hours IS A NUMBER
      `s 1173(1) the day is a working day for the company` IS A FUNCTION FROM DATE TO BOOLEAN
      `days still to search` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 1147 instant`
`s 1147(5) count the hours from the instant over working days only` MEANS
    IF `days still to search` LESS THAN 0
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): no working day within the days searched, so the working-day answer of s 1173(1) never lets the hours run out
    ELSE IF `s 1173(1) the day is a working day for the company` (start's `s 1147 day of the instant`)
         THEN IF hours AT MOST available
              THEN JUST (`s 1147 instant` OF (start's `s 1147 day of the instant`), (start's `s 1147 hour of the day` PLUS hours))
              ELSE `s 1147(5) count the hours from the instant over working days only`
                       (`s 1147 instant` OF ((start's `s 1147 day of the instant`) PLUS 1), 0)
                       (hours MINUS available)
                       `s 1173(1) the day is a working day for the company`
                       (`days still to search` MINUS 1)
         ELSE `s 1147(5) count the hours from the instant over working days only`
                  (`s 1147 instant` OF ((start's `s 1147 day of the instant`) PLUS 1), 0)
                  hours
                  `s 1173(1) the day is a working day for the company`
                  (`days still to search` MINUS 1)
    WHERE
        available MEANS 24 MINUS (start's `s 1147 hour of the day`)

-- The instant at which a period of hours ends. 24:00 on a day is written as 00:00 on the next day.
-- src:16329 | (5) In calculating a period of hours for the purposes of this section, no account shall be taken of any part of a day that is not a working day.
@ref s 1147(5) In calculating a period of hours, no account is taken of any part of a day that is not a working day (src:16329)
GIVEN start IS A `s 1147 instant`
      hours IS A NUMBER
      `s 1173(1) the day is a working day for the company` IS A FUNCTION FROM DATE TO BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 1147 instant`
`s 1147(5) the instant at which the period of hours ends` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 1147(5) count the hours from the instant over working days only` start hours `s 1173(1) the day is a working day for the company` 400
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): see the search limit above
    WHEN JUST end THEN
        IF end's `s 1147 hour of the day` EQUALS 24
        THEN JUST (`s 1147 instant` OF ((end's `s 1147 day of the instant`) PLUS 1), 0)
        ELSE JUST end

-- src:16318 | (2) Where—
-- src:16319 | (a) the document or information is sent by post (whether in hard copy or electronic form) to an address in the United Kingdom, and
-- src:16320 | (b) the company is able to show that it was properly addressed, prepaid and posted,
-- src:16321 | it is deemed to have been received by the intended recipient 48 hours after it was posted.
@ref s 1147(2) Document sent by post: deemed received 48 hours after it was posted (src:16318-16321)
GIVEN `the document or information is sent by post (whether in hard copy or electronic form) to an address in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is able to show that it was properly addressed, prepaid and posted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instant it was posted` IS A `s 1147 instant`
      `s 1173(1) the day is a working day for the company` IS A FUNCTION FROM DATE TO BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 1147 instant`
`s 1147(2) the instant at which the document or information is deemed received by post` MEANS
    IF `the document or information is sent by post (whether in hard copy or electronic form) to an address in the United Kingdom`
       AND `the company is able to show that it was properly addressed, prepaid and posted`
    THEN `s 1147(5) the instant at which the period of hours ends` `the instant it was posted` 48 `s 1173(1) the day is a working day for the company`
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where— (a) the document or information is sent by post (whether in hard copy or electronic form) to an address in the United Kingdom, and (b) the company is able to show that it was properly addressed, prepaid and posted"

-- src:16322 | (3) Where—
-- src:16323 | (a) the document or information is sent or supplied by electronic means, and
-- src:16324 | (b) the company is able to show that it was properly addressed,
-- src:16325 | it is deemed to have been received by the intended recipient 48 hours after it was sent.
@ref s 1147(3) Document sent by electronic means: deemed received 48 hours after it was sent (src:16322-16325)
GIVEN `the document or information is sent or supplied by electronic means` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is able to show that it was properly addressed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instant it was sent` IS A `s 1147 instant`
      `s 1173(1) the day is a working day for the company` IS A FUNCTION FROM DATE TO BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 1147 instant`
`s 1147(3) the instant at which the document or information is deemed received by electronic means` MEANS
    IF `the document or information is sent or supplied by electronic means`
       AND `the company is able to show that it was properly addressed`
    THEN `s 1147(5) the instant at which the period of hours ends` `the instant it was sent` 48 `s 1173(1) the day is a working day for the company`
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where— (a) the document or information is sent or supplied by electronic means, and (b) the company is able to show that it was properly addressed"

-- "when the material was first made available on the website, or (b) if later, when the recipient received (or is
-- deemed to have received) notice": the later of the two instants.
-- src:16326 | (4) Where the document or information is sent or supplied by means of a website, it is deemed to have been received by the intended recipient—
-- src:16327 | (a) when the material was first made available on the website, or
-- src:16328 | (b) if later, when the recipient received (or is deemed to have received) notice of the fact that the material was available on the website.
@ref s 1147(4) Document sent by means of a website (src:16326-16328)
GIVEN `the instant the material was first made available on the website` IS A `s 1147 instant`
      `the instant the recipient received or is deemed to have received notice that the material was available` IS A `s 1147 instant`
GIVETH A `s 1147 instant`
`s 1147(4) the instant at which the document or information is deemed received by means of a website` MEANS
    IF `the instant the recipient received or is deemed to have received notice that the material was available`'s `s 1147 day of the instant`
           GREATER THAN `the instant the material was first made available on the website`'s `s 1147 day of the instant`
       OR (    `the instant the recipient received or is deemed to have received notice that the material was available`'s `s 1147 day of the instant`
                   EQUALS `the instant the material was first made available on the website`'s `s 1147 day of the instant`
           AND `the instant the recipient received or is deemed to have received notice that the material was available`'s `s 1147 hour of the day`
                   GREATER THAN `the instant the material was first made available on the website`'s `s 1147 hour of the day`)
    THEN `the instant the recipient received or is deemed to have received notice that the material was available`
    ELSE `the instant the material was first made available on the website`

-- src:16316 | 1147 Deemed delivery of documents and information
-- src:16317 | (1) This section applies in relation to documents and information sent or supplied by a company.
@ref s 1147(1) Deemed delivery: documents and information sent or supplied by a company (src:16316-16317)
GIVEN `the deemed instant under subsection (2), (3) or (4)` IS A MAYBE `s 1147 instant`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 1147 the day the document is treated as delivered` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the deemed instant under subsection (2), (3) or (4)`
    WHEN JUST instant THEN JUST (instant's `s 1147 day of the instant`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): none of the three deeming rules of subsections (2), (3) and (4) applies on the facts

DECLARE `s 1147 capacity of the recipient` IS ONE OF
    `s 1147 a member`
    `s 1147 a holder of the company's debentures`
    `s 1147 a person otherwise than in the capacity of a member or debenture holder`

-- src:16330 | (6) This section has effect subject to—
-- src:16331 | (a) in its application to documents or information sent or supplied by a company to its members, any contrary provision of the company's articles;
-- src:16332 | (b) in its application to documents or information sent or supplied by a company to its debentures holders, any contrary provision in the instrument constituting the debentures;
-- src:16333 | (c) in its application to documents or information sent or supplied by a company to a person otherwise than in his capacity as a member or debenture holder, any contrary provision in an agreement between the company and that person.
@ref s 1147(6) The section is subject to a contrary provision of the articles, the debenture instrument or an agreement (src:16330-16333)
GIVEN capacity IS A `s 1147 capacity of the recipient`
      `the articles contain a contrary provision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instrument constituting the debentures contains a contrary provision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an agreement between the company and the person contains a contrary provision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1147(6) the deeming rules yield to the contrary provision` MEANS
    CONSIDER capacity
    WHEN `s 1147 a member` THEN
        IF `the articles contain a contrary provision`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in its application to documents or information sent or supplied by a company to its members, any contrary provision of the company's articles"
    WHEN `s 1147 a holder of the company's debentures` THEN
        IF `the instrument constituting the debentures contains a contrary provision`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to its debentures holders, any contrary provision in the instrument constituting the debentures"
    WHEN `s 1147 a person otherwise than in the capacity of a member or debenture holder` THEN
        IF `an agreement between the company and the person contains a contrary provision`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to a person otherwise than in his capacity as a member or debenture holder, any contrary provision in an agreement between the company and that person"

-- ---- s 1148: Interpretation of company communications provisions ----------------------------------------

-- src:16335 | (1) In the company communications provisions—
-- src:16336 | “address” includes a number or address used for the purposes of sending or receiving documents or information by electronic means;
@ref s 1148(1) "Address" in the company communications provisions (src:16335-16336)
GIVEN `it is a number or address used for the purposes of sending or receiving documents or information by electronic means` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1148(1) the thing is an address` MEANS
    IF `it is a number or address used for the purposes of sending or receiving documents or information by electronic means`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“address” includes a number or address used for the purposes of sending or receiving documents or information by electronic means"

-- src:16335 | (1) In the company communications provisions—
-- src:16337 | “company” includes any body corporate;
@ref s 1148(1) "Company" in the company communications provisions (src:16335-16337)
GIVEN `s 1173(1) the person is a body corporate or a corporation` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1148(1) the body is a company` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 1173(1) the person is a body corporate or a corporation`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“company” includes any body corporate"

DECLARE `s 1148 kind of document` IS ONE OF
    `s 1148 a summons`
    `s 1148 a notice`
    `s 1148 an order`
    `s 1148 other legal process`
    `s 1148 a register`
    `s 1148 any other document`

-- src:16335 | (1) In the company communications provisions—
-- src:16338 | “document” includes summons, notice, order or other legal process and registers.
@ref s 1148(1) "Document" in the company communications provisions (src:16335-16338)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 1148 kind of document`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1148(1) the thing is a document` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 1148 any other document` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“document” includes summons, notice, order or other legal process and registers": the list is not closed
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:16339 | (2) References in the company communications provisions to provisions of the Companies Acts authorising or requiring a document or information to be sent or supplied include all such provisions, whatever expression is used, and references to documents or information being sent or supplied shall be construed accordingly.
@ref s 1148(2) References to provisions authorising or requiring documents or information to be sent or supplied (src:16339)
GIVEN `the provision of the Companies Acts authorises or requires a document or information to be sent or supplied` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1148(2) the reference includes the provision, whatever expression is used` MEANS
    IF `the provision of the Companies Acts authorises or requires a document or information to be sent or supplied`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "References ... include all such provisions, whatever expression is used"

-- src:16340 | (3) References in the company communications provisions to documents or information being sent or supplied by or to a company include references to documents or information being sent or supplied by or to the directors of a company acting on behalf of the company.
@ref s 1148(3) References to documents or information sent or supplied by or to the directors acting on behalf of the company (src:16340)
GIVEN `the document or information is sent or supplied by or to the directors of a company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors are acting on behalf of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1148(3) the reference to sending or supplying by or to a company includes the case` MEANS
    IF `the document or information is sent or supplied by or to the directors of a company` AND `the directors are acting on behalf of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "References ... include references to documents or information being sent or supplied by or to the directors of a company acting on behalf of the company"
